="pb-16">   <section id="overview" class="mg-col pt-16 sm:pt-20"> <div class="mg-title mb-8"> <p class="font-lato text-[12px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-[rgba(0,0,0,0.6)]"> The short answer </p> <h2 class="mg-serif mt-1.5 text-[30px] font-bold leading-[1.12] sm:text-[36px] tracking-[-0.012em] text-[#1e293b]"> Little River Airbnb Market at a Glance </h2>  </div> <div class="mg-prose"> <p id="introduction-earning-shape">Rates and bookings both trail the South Carolina average. Listings averaged <strong>$200</strong> a night and were booked on <strong>34%</strong> of available nights, against $355 and 39% for the South Carolina average.</p><p id="introduction-seasonality">Timing matters: in <strong>July</strong>, usually the best month, the average listing earns about 2.8 times as much as in <strong>November</strong>, usually the slowest.</p><p id="introduction-market-context">With 169 active listings, Little River is the 30th-largest of 116 South Carolina markets AirROI tracks. From a year earlier, average revenue rose 19% while the number of active listings grew 56%.</p> </div> <a href="/atlas/map?country-code=US&#38;state=South-Carolina&#38;city=Little-River" rel="nofollow" class="pseo-atlas group relative block min-h-[76px] overflow-hidden rounded-[4px] font-lato mt-8"> <img src="https://airroi.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/public/assets/cities/United%20States/South%20Carolina/Little%20River.png" alt="Map of Airbnb listings in Little River" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105"> <span class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-r from-slate-950/85 via-slate-900/55 to-slate-900/20"></span> <span class="relative flex min-h-[76px] items-center px-5 py-3 text-white"> <span class="flex-1"> <span class="block text-[15px] font-bold">Browse the live Little River Airbnb market</span> <span class="mt-0.5 hidden text-[12.5px] text-slate-300 sm:block">Search by revenue,