t in Myrtle Beach? </h2>  </div> <div class="mg-report prose max-w-none">  <div id="monthly-rates"> <p>The average nightly rate in Myrtle Beach, known as ADR (average daily rate), was <strong>$257</strong> over the past year, about 28% below the South Carolina average of $355 and about 20% below the U.S. average of $320. In a typical year, rates swing with the seasons, from about $180 in November and December to about $320 in July.</p><p>The top 10% charge about 2.5 times the rate of the bottom quarter.</p><ul class="not-prose my-5 space-y-1.5"><li><span aria-hidden="true" class="mr-2.5 inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-[2px] align-[0.05em]" style="background-color:#5f5ab8"></span><span class="font-semibold text-[#1e293b]">Best-in-class properties</span> (top 10%) charge <strong>$400+</strong> a night, about twice the median.</li><li><span aria-hidden="true" class="mr-2.5 inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-[2px] align-[0.05em]" style="background-color:#8884d8"></span><span class="font-semibold text-[#1e293b]">Strong performers</span> (top 25%) charge <strong>$285</strong> or more, about $75 above the median.</li><li><span aria-hidden="true" class="mr-2.5 inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-[2px] align-[0.05em]" style="background-color:#b3b0e6"></span><span class="font-semibold text-[#1e293b]">Typical properties</span> (median) charge about <strong>$210</strong> a night.</li><li><span aria-hidden="true" class="mr-2.5 inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-[2px] align-[0.05em]" style="background-color:#dddcf5"></span><span class="font-semibold text-[#1e293b]">Entry-level properties</span> (bottom 25%) charge <strong>$160</strong> or less, about three-quarters of the median.</li></ul><div class="not-prose my-8"><figure class="pseo-figure font-lato rounded-[4px] bg-white shadow-[0_1px_2px_rgba(15,23,42,0.06),0_3px_14px_rgba(15,23,42,0.07)] p-5 sm:p-6 [&#38;_.pseo-table]:shadow-none"> <figcaption> <p class="text-[16px] font-bold leading-snug text-[#1e293b]">July rates run 79% above 